WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.063
India's cheetahs didn't just

2
00:00:02.063 --> 00:00:02.710
come back.

3
00:00:03.035 --> 00:00:04.932
A court had to say yes first.

4
00:00:05.212 --> 00:00:07.079
The cheetah was declared

5
00:00:07.079 --> 00:00:09.024
extinct in India in 1952.

6
00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:11.429
In January 2020, the Supreme

7
00:00:11.429 --> 00:00:13.677
Court allowed African cheetahs

8
00:00:13.677 --> 00:00:15.978
to be brought to a suitable habitat.

9
00:00:16.312 --> 00:00:18.521
It called this an introduction,

10
00:00:18.521 --> 00:00:20.089
not a re-introduction,

11
00:00:20.645 --> 00:00:22.276
and set up an expert committee

12
00:00:22.276 --> 00:00:22.929
to guide it.

13
00:00:23.311 --> 00:00:25.241
The first eight came from Namibia,

14
00:00:25.839 --> 00:00:28.560
released at Kuno in September 2022.

15
00:00:28.966 --> 00:00:31.218
Twelve more came from South

16
00:00:31.218 --> 00:00:32.469
Africa in 2023.

17
00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:35.273
As of September 2026, India

18
00:00:35.273 --> 00:00:37.473
has over fifty cheetahs,

19
00:00:37.844 --> 00:00:39.183
most of them born here.

20
00:00:39.515 --> 00:00:40.571
Permission came first.

21
00:00:41.058 --> 00:00:42.163
The work came after.

22
00:00:42.586 --> 00:00:43.079
Your turn.

23
00:00:43.468 --> 00:00:44.650
Where did the first cheetahs

24
00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:45.072
come from?
